**Convention 1.3 (credited finite factors and canonical alphabet).**
Use the temporal factor and canonicalization of [FMR, Section 2][FMR]
and [RRN, Section 7][RRN]. A factor is written $(b,c)$. For a branch
endpoint it is $(0,0)$. If $q=ar$ first meets an original leaf
$\ell$ at $a$, put $e(\alpha)=0$, $e(\beta)=1$ and
$s(r)=\#L(r)+2\#R(r)$, and set

$$
\Gamma_q(u)=
\begin{cases}
(2-e(\ell),1-e(\ell)),&r=\varepsilon,\\
(s(r)+2-e(\ell),\mathbf1_{\{r\text{ ends in }R\}}),&r\ne\varepsilon.
\end{cases}
\tag{WBF.2}
$$

The credited exact decoder on attained factors is

$$
\operatorname{Pred}((b,c),k)=
\begin{cases}
\mathsf{branch},&k\ge b,\\
\beta,&b\ge1\text{ and }k=b-1,\\
\alpha,&c=1\text{ and }k=b-2,\\
\mathsf{absent},&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
\tag{WBF.3}
$$

It equals $r_{\rho^ku}(q)$, including initially absent targets.
The entire trajectory determines $b$ by its first branch count and
$c$ by its alpha stage. Let $C_0=\langle\alpha,\alpha\rangle$ and

$$
S_1=\{\alpha,\beta,C_0\},\qquad
S_{d+1}=\{\alpha,\beta\}\sqcup
\{\langle x,y\rangle:x,y\in S_d\}.
\tag{WBF.4}
$$

For $\operatorname{ht}(v)\le d$, the canonical completion
$\pi_d(v)$ retains constructors through depth $d-1$ and replaces
a branch at that depth by $C_0$. It belongs to $S_d$, fixes $S_d$,
and preserves every reply and factor on $W_d$. In particular
$|S_3|=123$. These are reused exact finite suppliers, not new
factor or canonicalization theorems.

